# Docker builds happen only for the update-api service, and the build context is
# the repository root. Ship nothing else: the Android app carries a full Linux
# rootfs inside jniLibs, so a whole-repo context would transfer hundreds of
# megabytes on every deploy.
*

!update-api
update-api/data/
update-api/tmp-live/
update-api/tmp-smoke/
update-api/tmp-*.out
update-api/bin/
update-api/scripts/
update-api/*.db
update-api/*.db-*
update-api/*.apk
update-api/*.exe
update-api/*.out
update-api/.env
update-api/.env.*
update-api/Dockerfile
update-api/.dockerignore
update-api/*.md

# Re-included because the landing page reads it, and the module needs its deps.
!update-api/.env.example
!update-api/go.mod
!update-api/go.sum
